{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"paralytic-yester-needletail","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Land PR #128 safe subset via Gerrit: json-repair 0.63.0 + genai-prices 0.1.2 + botocore 1.43.69; mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b (4th re-proposal)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror: dependabot PRs never merge there; content is re-applied\nlocally and landed via Gerrit, then the PR is closed. PR #128 (branch\n`dependabot/uv/uv-lock-bfcc8af838`) proposes 4 uv-lock updates:\n\n* `mcp` `1.29.0` -> `2.0.0` (MAJOR) — the FOURTH re-proposal (PRs #124/#125/#127),\n  rejected each time under ticket 1dfd-…: mcp 2.0 renames `FastMCP` -> `MCPServer`,\n  replaces transport+`ClientSession`+`initialize()` with `Client`, splits types into\n  `mcp-types`, and diverts stdout while serving — all breaking for `mcp_server.py` +\n  `gen_mcp_reference.py`. Migration is epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b`; the pyproject\n  ceiling stays `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` (core L22 floor via `[mcp]` extra L82 + agents L215).\n  NEW urgency fact (recorded on 732b as part of this work): v2.0.0 is now the STABLE\n  release and v1.x is in maintenance mode (security fixes only), so `<2` is\n  time-bounded — but that changes the epic's priority, not this ticket's scope.\n* `json-repair` `0.62.0` -> `0.63.0` (minor) — SAFE. Usage surface:\n  `src/rebar/llm/structured.py` calls `repair_json(cand, return_objects=True[, schema=…])`\n  (L387-408); 0.63.0 adds None->null repair + fixes a `TrueBlue` mis-repair — both\n  strictly improve the tolerant-parse ladder; the called API is unchanged. pyproject\n  floor `json-repair>=0.61` (L132) already admits it: LOCK-ONLY.\n* `genai-prices` `0.1.1` -> `0.1.2` (patch) — SAFE. Pricing-data-only additions (new\n  model prices); consumed via optional lazy import in `usage_report.py`/`usage_log.py`\n  (`Usage` + `calc_price`, unchanged). pyproject has no pin (L150): LOCK-ONLY.\n* `botocore` `1.43.68` -> `1.43.69` (patch) — SAFE. Routine service-model update;\n  lazy imports only (`bedrock_model.py`, `structured.py`, `remote_cert.py`). Floor\n  `botocore>=1.43.0` (L291) admits it; boto3 1.43.68's botocore range (`<1.44`)\n  accepts 1.43.69, so boto3 itself need not move: LOCK-ONLY.\n\nThis ticket lands the three safe bumps only. No new mcp migration ticket is filed —\nepic 732b already owns it (per the #125/#127 precedent, tickets\ncarnivoral-consistent-lhasaapso and reclinable-ammonitic-hound / change 1812).\n\n## Approach\n\nIn a fresh worktree branched from `origin/main` (`../deps-128`, venv on PATH):\n\n1. NO pyproject.toml edit — verify with `git diff` that all three bumps are admitted\n   by existing constraints (floors listed above; exact pins exist for none of them).\n2. `uv lock --upgrade-package json-repair --upgrade-package genai-prices\n   --upgrade-package botocore` — the lock is regenerated by uv, never hand-edited\n   (CI gates on `uv lock --check`); then `uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra agents`\n   so gates run against the bumped versions.\n3. Verify the lock moved exactly the three intended packages to the PR's versions\n   (0.63.0 / 0.1.2 / 1.43.69) and `mcp` stayed 1.29.0; `git diff uv.lock` must show\n   no other version churn beyond uv's transitive bookkeeping for these three.\n4. Gates: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `uv lock --check`, and targeted tests for\n   each usage surface: `pytest tests/unit/test_structured.py\n   tests/unit/test_silent_success.py tests/unit/test_usage_log.py\n   tests/unit/test_usage_log_pricing_qualified_2ca9.py` (json-repair + genai-prices\n   consumers) plus `tests/unit/test_llm_capabilities.py` if present (botocore lazy\n   import). Full `pytest tests/unit` is CI's job (host has pre-existing env git\n   failures documented on dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61); CI Verified +1 is the authoritative\n   full-suite gate.\n5. Commit (subject <=50 chars, body wrapped at 72) with trailer\n   `rebar-ticket: <this ticket's full canonical id>` + DCO `-s`;\n   `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`. Leave the ticket in_progress for the bots;\n   the change is submitted only after LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.\n6. Comment on PR #128 (mcp rejected again per 732b, citing #124/#125/#127; safe\n   subset landing via the new Gerrit change); comment the v2-stable/v1-maintenance\n   urgency fact on epic 732b. Do NOT close the PR.\n\n## STOP / defer rule (explicit fallback done-state)\n\nIf ANY of the three bumps fails its targeted tests or lint/typecheck in step 4:\ndrop ONLY that package from the bump (re-run `uv lock --upgrade-package …` with the\nremaining packages from a clean `git checkout uv.lock`), record the failure evidence\nas a ticket comment, and land the remaining safe packages. The fallback done-state is\nAC2b: the ticket closes legitimately with a PARTIAL subset landed, provided every\ndropped package has a recorded-on-ticket failure reason. If ALL three fail, the\ndone-state is the recorded evidence plus no lock change pushed (abandon the change,\ncomment the outcome; the ticket then closes on AC2b's evidence path with zero landed).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n* mcp 2.0 migration (epic 732b) — the ceiling `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` is untouched.\n* boto3 version bump — not in PR #128 and not required by botocore 1.43.69.\n* Any src/rebar code change — nothing in the three deltas requires one.\n* `.github/complexity-baseline.json` — never touched by a deps change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `uv.lock` on merged main records json-repair 0.63.0, genai-prices 0.1.2,\n  botocore 1.43.69 (or a documented AC2b subset), with mcp still 1.29.0 and\n  pyproject.toml unchanged; `uv lock --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC2: targeted usage-surface tests pass against the bumped versions\n  (test_structured.py, test_silent_success.py, test_usage_log.py,\n  test_usage_log_pricing_qualified_2ca9.py), and `make lint` + `make typecheck`\n  exit 0.\n- [ ] AC2b (fallback path): every package dropped under the STOP rule has a ticket\n  comment recording the concrete failure evidence and the re-lock excluding it; the\n  landed subset satisfies AC1 for the packages it retains. (Vacuously satisfied when\n  all three land.)\n- [ ] AC3: the change lands through Gerrit with a `rebar-ticket:` trailer for this\n  ticket's full canonical id + DCO sign-off, after LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.\n- [ ] AC4: PR #128 carries a comment citing epic 732b + prior PRs #124/#125/#127 for\n  the mcp rejection and pointing at the Gerrit change; the PR is left open.\n- [ ] AC5: epic 732b-51df-acf2-477b carries a comment recording that mcp v2.0.0 is\n  the stable release and v1.x is maintenance-mode (security fixes only), i.e. the\n  `<2` ceiling is now time-bounded.\n- [ ] AC6: this ticket records a relates_to link to dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61\n  (reclinable-ammonitic-hound, the #127 precedent).","id":"c44a-2d4c-f793-42e6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"deps: PR #128 safe subset (json-repair 0.63.0, genai-prices 0.1.2, botocore 1.43.69); mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786823914792440001,"uuid":"e8e3c52c-0273-49cc-be68-38414b490f67"}